AB  - This paper addresses sparse observability constraints in Diffusion Least Mean Squares (DLMS) and proposes a framework for analyzing combination strategies. A thresholding-based algorithm is introduced to identify the sparse support vector under incomplete information. The method effectively handles sparse observations in both time and transform domains, achieving a 30-40 dB improvement in Mean Square Deviation (MSD) over conventional DLMS.
