AB  - In this paper, we propose a novel clustered multitask diffusion RLS (MT-DRLS) algorithm over network to further improve the performance of its counterpart, the multitask diffusion LMS (MT-DLMS) algorithm. Its transient behavior is investigated, in the mean and mean-square error sense. Simulation results illustrate the significant improvement of the MT-DRLS over the MT-DLMS in terms of convergence rate and steady-state error, as well as the accuracy of the theoretical findings.
