AB  - The problem of distributed adaptive filtering is considered in this paper, where all the nodes in the network will estimate an unknown parameter from noisy measurements cooperatively. In this work, we mainly focus on consensus strategies and normalized least mean squares (NLMS)-based adaptive filters, where the network is described by directed and Markovian switching graphs. The stability results of the above distributed adaptive filters are established under directed Markovian switching networks and a general cooperative information assumption, without independence and stationarity signal conditions which are widely used in the literature. Moreover, the stability results also indicate that even any node can not estimate the unknown parameter individually, the estimation task can still be fulfilled through local communications among nodes in the network.
