AB  - In this paper, we propose a multitask diffusion average bias-compensated LMS (M-DABC-LMS) algorithm to address the challenges caused by noisy inputs, outputs, and communication links in multitask networks. The algorithm first applies a bias-compensation strategy to mitigate input noise and then employs an average-based denoising technique to handle communication noise. To further improve resilience against adversarial attacks, we extend this framework to a secure version, termed SM-DABC-LMS, which incorporates a mean-subsequence-reduction (MSR) strategy. We analyze the mean and mean-square behavior of the proposed algorithms, and simulation results demonstrate that they achieve up to 6 dB lower mean-square deviation (MSD) compared to conventional multitask diffusion methods.
