AB  - In this paper, a multitask diffusion average bias-compensation least mean-square (M-DABC-LMS) algorithm is proposed, aiming to address the problem of noise interference in multitask networks. The algorithm comprises the following steps: the bias-compensation strategy is utilized in the adaptive updating phase; the weight bias caused by communication link noise is handled by the denoising average-estimation technique; and the custom adaptive combination coefficients are utilized in the combination step. To address the limited information available at each node in the early stages of the M-DABC-LMS algorithm, the multitask diffusion mixed average-estimation bias-compensation LMS(M-DMABC-LMS) algorithm is further designed to accelerate the convergence of the algorithm by incorporating an adaptive mixing factor. Finally, the proposed algorithms are verified by simulation to outperform other conventional multitask diffusion least mean-square algorithms.
