TI  - A Study of Emotion-based Music Generation using Diffusion Model
T2  - 2024 JOINT 13TH INTERNATIONAL CONFERENCE ON SOFT COMPUTING AND INTELLIGENT SYSTEMS AND 25TH INTERNATIONAL SYMPOSIUM ON ADVANCED INTELLIGENT SYSTEMS, SCIS&ISIS
LA  - English
CP  - 2024 Joint International Conference on Soft Computing and Intelligent Systems and International Symposium on Advanced Intelligent Systems
AB  - This research aims to develop a method that can generate a variety of music using a diffusion model, taking emotion as input and controlling it by musical attributes corresponding to the emotion as an approach to music generation. The diffusion model uses a method called Diffusion Language Model, which can control the generation of music by using a classifier at each time denoising stage, and the classifier identifies emotions using musical attribute values. Experiments were conducted to compare the music generated when the learning method and classifier were changed for the proposed method, and to evaluate whether the music reflected emotion or not. The results of the experiment did not confirm that music was generated for the input emotion, but did confirm that the characteristics of the generated music could be controlled by devising the learning method and classifier processing.
