AB  - Hybrid text-to-speech (TTS) systems that integrate a language model with flow matching decoders have been proposed to generate speech in voice-related applications such as dubbing. However, these systems suffer from latency and computational overhead caused by next-token prediction and denoising steps. Therefore, we propose an uncluttered hybrid TTS system that integrates a lightweight flow matching decoder and supports variable token prediction time. In addition, we leverage a training strategy from a diffusion-based approach into the language model to enhance its generative performance. The results of objective and subjective evaluations demonstrate that our proposed method is significantly more efficient than existing hybrid systems while maintaining competitive speech quality.
