AB  - One of the biggest challenges humanity faces is climate change, which requires new ideas when analysing, predicting, and mitigating. The convergence of Big Data Analytics and Generative Artificial Intelligence offers numerous benefits in combating these threats, including improved climate modelling, enhanced evaluation accuracy, and decision-making support systems. In this research, we provide a detailed overview of utilising Big Data Analytics with Generative AI for Climate Change. We classify current methods based on data source, generative AI domains, and applicable methodology. The proposed taxonomy encompasses climate modelling methods utilising Generator Adversarial Networks, large language models for climate language and analysis, a diffusion-based model for generating imitation society scenarios, and a transformed architecture for integrating temporal climate models. We present 150+ research papers and share some collected metrics, datasets, and computational systems. Moreover, we highlight some existing flaws, including insufficient data availability, complex computational architecture, misinterpreted model evaluation, and a lack of interdisciplinary integration. This survey concludes with some research directions, highlighting real-time analytical solutions, liberal learning methodologies, understandable artificial intelligence integration, and developed Decision support systems for climate policy.
