AB  - This article presents Revolver, a 28 nm low-bit GenAI accelerator for distilled large language models (LLMs), chain-of-thought (CoT)-enabled reasoning, multi-turn chat, and diffusion-model generation. Modern compact GenAI models improve quality through distillation and CoT but become more sensitive to low-bit quantization and require different precisions across inference phases. Revolver addresses this with three hardware-algorithm co-optimizations: phase-aware precision selection (PAPS) with multi-precision residual encoding (MPRE), local rotation with harmonic-aligned permutation (LR-HAP) and paired unit-FHT block (PUB), and sliced integer-based dequantization unit (SIDU). PAPS + MPRE reduces system energy by 50.4% by applying high-precision (HP) only to sensitive phases and compressing multi-precision weights. LR-HAP + PUB enables fast Hadamard transform (FHT)-only rotation for non-power-of-two (non-PoT) channel sizes and reduces rotation-unit power/area by 59.4%/60.8%. SIDU realizes asymmetric per-group quantization with fully integer dequantization, reducing processing element (PE) power/area by 45.1%/43.1%. Fabricated in Samsung 28 nm CMOS, Revolver achieves 16.4 TOPS and 13.7 TOPS/W in INT4 mode. It provides up to 2.10 & times; LLM decode speedup on LLaMA3-8B distilled CoT reasoning and up to 3.47 & times; energy saving on PixArt-Sigma diffusion generation while maintaining accuracy within 2.0%p and 0.42 HPS-v2 points, respectively.
