AB  - With the proposal of the carbon peaking and carbon neutrality, high proportion of new energy sources and power electronic devices are more and more integrated into power systems. In this situation, a series of oscillation problems have been triggered. Eigenvalue analysis is one of effective methods for studying oscillations in power systems. However, for eigenvalue analysis based on continuous state space, the modeling may become complex when topology changes. In this paper, two discrete state space forms are built for typical RLC electric circuits. One is modeled by separate RLC element, and the other is implemented by merged RL and RC models. Subsequently, four typical circuits are selected to verify the consistency, by comparing actual eigenvalues derived from two discrete forms.
