KW  - Learning (artificial intelligence)
KW  - Quantitative trading
KW  - large language models
KW  - flow matching
KW  - continuous normalizing flows
KW  - interpretable AI
AB  - Quantitative trading systems powered by artificial intelligence face dual critical challenges: the opacity of decision-making processes that violate regulatory transparency requirements, and excessive portfolio turnover stemming from point-wise action generation that ignores temporal dependencies-issues that existing approaches cannot simultaneously resolve while maintaining competitive returns. This paper presents FLA (Financial-Language-Action), a novel framework that integrates large language models with flow-matching networks to achieve interpretable, temporally coherent trading strategies through language-grounded semantic reasoning and continuous trajectory synthesis. The framework introduces four key innovations: (1) Multi-modal Financial Scene Encoder leveraging cross-modal attention and chain-of-thought supervision to produce semantically grounded representations from numerical market features and textual contextual information, (2) Latent Space Alignment via auxiliary value prediction and contrastive learning to ensure condition vectors encode predictive information about future returns, (3) Flow Matching Action Generator synthesizing multi-step action chunks with explicit trajectory-level smoothness regularization and turnover penalties to reduce transaction costs, and (4) Three-Stage Training Curriculum that progressively builds interpretability, temporal coherence, and market adaptability while freezing components to prevent catastrophic forgetting. Theoretical analysis establishes provable guarantees on trajectory smoothness, with O(1/K) reduction in transaction cost and bounded semantic-action consistency. Extensive experiments on three financial markets (DJIA, CSI 300, Cryptocurrency) spanning 2016-2023 demonstrate state-of-the-art Sharpe ratios of 1.26 +/- 0.02 , 1.13 +/- 0.03 , and 1.01 +/- 0.04 , respectively, while achieving 43%, 43%, and 32% reductions in maximum drawdown compared to market indices. Ablation studies reveal that flow-matching-based trajectory generation provides 18.9% improvement in Sharpe ratio over diffusion policies. At the same time, the complete architecture delivers 15-28% portfolio turnover reduction, validating practical deployment viability across diverse market regimes with superior risk-adjusted performance and interpretability.
