KW  - diffusion models
KW  - energy-efficient hardware
KW  - word alignment
AB  - As AI models grow in scale, their intensive computation raises energy concerns. Floating-point compute-in-memory (FP-CIM) architectures offer a promising path for training-heavy tasks like large language models, diffusion generation, and object detection. However, existing designs often face challenges in accuracy, efficiency, or scalability. This work proposes a 28nm word-aligned FP-CIM macro optimized for CNN training and diffusion models. Featuring a four-stage MAC pipeline, low-bit-skip Wallace-tree multiplier, and adaptive dual-function shifter, it balances power, performance, and area. Operating at 0.45-0.9V, the macro achieves 37.2 TFLOPS/W and 72.96% VGG16 accuracy on CIFAR100, along with 10.57 FIP on a Celeb-A diffusion task. It outperforms prior works by up to 26.15x in combined energy, area, and accuracy.
