AB  - Compact subspaces of function spaces with the shift flow figure prominently into the study of dynamical systems where the evolution variable (usually time) is R,Z,R+ or Z(+), i.e. continuous or discrete flows or semi-flows. Many important theories depend on this compactness. Up to this point theorems guaranteeing compactness have been limited to three function spaces. These are the functions continuous on R with the topology of uniform convergence on compact subsets of R, the space L-loc(p)(R) with the L-loc(p)(R) topology and finally the non metrizable space L-loc(infinity)(R) with an induced weak* topology. In this publication we introduce a new metric that takes e.g. unbounded rapidly oscillatory functions and shows that their hulls are compact in the shift flow. This extends the results obtained in the 1970's on Lifting Theorems and Spectral Theory by the author and George Sell, as well as any application involving a compact dynamical system.
