AB  - The representation of a discrete state space in a quantum machine can be very effective due to the superposition effect, where n qubits represent 2(n) states. To the authors' knowledge, the Bayesian update step using a quantum computing regime has been unsolved up to date. In this paper, a quantum realization of the Daum-Huang log-homotopy flow filter is presented as a solution of the filtering step in a Bayesian recursion for state estimation. The numerical example for a low-dimensional problem demonstrates the feasibility of the presented approach.
