AB  - In order to improve the efficiency of wave energy generation within the constraints of real working conditions, model predictive control (MPC) strategy for the direct drive wave energy converter (WEC) was studied. By establishing the discrete state space model of direct drive WEC, the prediction process and objective function of MPC are further deduced, and the constraints of system variables are incorporated into the optimal control to solve the optimal control quantity. Finally, simulation was carried out considering different constraints, it is proved that the effectiveness of MPC is better than that of the conventional control strategies, and the system state variables are more in line with the actual working conditions.
