AB  - In this paper, duality theory for hidden Markov models (HMMs) in discrete-time and discrete-state-space settings is presented. The study focuses on HMMs with binary-valued observations to facilitate interpretability and understanding, making it useful for pedagogical purposes. The paper includes two original contributions: (i) a dual control system for the HMM, formulated as a backward stochastic difference equation (BS Delta E), is presented; and (ii) a duality principle, demonstrating that a specific stochastic optimal control problem for the BS.E serves as the dual to the nonlinear filtering problem for the HMM, is described. Additionally, an explicit formula for optimal control is shown, leading to a novel type of nonlinear predictor for the HMM.
