TI  - Robust Linearly Constrained Kalman Filter for General Mismatched Linear State-Space Models
T2  - IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON AUTOMATIC CONTROL
LA  - English
KW  - Distortionless
KW  - linearly constrained Kalman filter (LCKF)
KW  - mitigation
KW  - model mismatch
KW  - robust filtering
KW  - robustness
KW  - DISCRETE
KW  - SYSTEMS
AB  - It is well known that Wiener filter and Kalman filter (KF) like techniques are sensitive to misspecified covariances, uncertainties in the system matrices, filter initialization, or unwanted system behaviors. A possible solution to robustify these estimation techniques is to impose linear constraints (LCs). In this article: 1) we introduce a general class of linearly constrained KF (LCKF), where a set of nonstationary LCs can be set at every time step; 2) explore the use of such LCs to mitigate modeling errors in general mismatched linear discrete state-space models; and 3) provide the theoretical formulation to show that the gain-constrained KF is a particular instance of the proposed LCKF. Because such LCs can be taken into account in any KF generalization, this sets the basis for a new robust filtering framework. An illustrative example is provided to support the discussion.
