TI  - Inertia Estimation Method for VSG-Dominated Power System Based on Improved Extended Kalman Filter
T2  - 2024 10TH INTERNATIONAL CONFERENCE ON POWER ELECTRONICS SYSTEMS AND APPLICATIONS, PESA 2024
LA  - English
CP  - 10th International Conference on Power Electronics Systems and Applications (PESA)
KW  - inertia estimation
KW  - improved extended Kalman filter
KW  - virtual synchronous machine
KW  - VSG-dominated power system
AB  - This paper proposes a method to estimate the inertia of power system dominated by virtual synchronous generators (VSGs) using an improved extended Kalman filter (EKF). Initially, the swing equation is reformulated into a discrete state-space equation incorporating parameters and noise effects. Then, during power system disturbances, signal preprocessing is applied to active power and frequency data measured by phasor measurement units (PMUs) at the VSG terminal bus. Finally, the grey wolf optimization (GWO) algorithm and U-D Filtering algorithm are integrated into the EKF algorithm. Compared to traditional methods of inertia constant estimation, this approach not only accurately estimates the virtual inertia constant of VSGs but also enables the estimation of virtual damping coefficients. Moreover, relative to direct parameter estimation using EKF, the algorithm enhances identification accuracy and robustness. The effectiveness of the method is validated through simulations on a VSG-dominated IEEE 9-bus power system.
