AB  - this work proposes a real-time multivariable adaptive robust control based on an embedded controller. The designed controller is evaluated over a twin rotor MIMO system by considering an eigenstructure assignment approach for its design in state space. The controller structure considers a full state observer for state estimation, where the design of the observer is also developed based on the eigenstructure assignment. The method's robustness stands in the good selection of the eigenvector subspaces corresponding to each closed loop eigenvalue. It is worth noting that the twin rotor MIMO system is a nonlinear system that is identified using the MOESP subspace approach for multivariable model identification in order to obtain a linear multivariable discrete state-space model. The proposed approach is compared with two PID structures using decoupling and coupled approaches. The robust controller is evaluated over a twin rotor MIMO simulation and an embedded C2000 Texas Instruments F28379d processor.
