AB  - This study proposes a human-computer collaborative packaging design process based on artificial intelligence. It leverages artificial intelligence and human-computer collaboration to improve design efficiency and accuracy, and provides empirical validation using biscuit packaging design as an example. First, we used Python web crawlers to collect 45,976 user reviews from major Chinese e-commerce platforms. After data cleaning and preprocessing, we obtained 33,283 valid review texts. Second, the Biterm Topic Model was used to extract 14 core design requirement topics from the review texts. Third, the design requirements were quantitatively weighted and prioritized using the Analytic Hierarchy Process. The results showed that the "Product identification and visual communication" dimension had the highest weight (0.5110), with "Premium texture and color scheme" being the most critical sub-criterion (global weight 0.1353). Fourth, using ChatGPT, we transformed key requirements into structured prompts. Two strategies, namely pure text generation and reference image generation, were implemented in three artificial intelligence generated content tools: Midjourney, Stable Diffusion, and DALL-E 2, resulting in a total of 6 candidate solutions. Finally, the VlseKriterijumska Optimizacija I Kompromisno Resenje multi-criteria decision-making method was introduced to select the optimal solution (Scheme 4), and the detailed design from die-cutting to three-dimensional rendering was completed. The results show that this method integrates big data mining, generative artificial intelligence and multi-criteria decision-making, and constructs a complete closed loop from user data to production-ready documents. While ensuring design quality, it bridges the gap between creativity and implementation, demonstrating the synergistic advantages of human-computer co-creation in design efficiency and accuracy, and providing a new technical framework and empirical reference for intelligent packaging design research.
