TI  - Optimized day trading via reinforcement learning and technical analysis using attention-LSTM, CNN, and explainable state modeling
T2  - INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF MACHINE LEARNING AND CYBERNETICS
LA  - English
KW  - Algorithmic trading
KW  - Q-learning
KW  - Technical analysis
KW  - Stock market trading
KW  - Explainable AI
KW  - STOCK
AB  - Developing an efficient state representation is a key challenge in implementing reinforcement learning for day trading, as it must accurately capture the market's key dynamics. This paper presents a dynamic trading system based on reinforcement learning, using technical indicators and chart patterns. A Q-learning agent is trained on a new state representation that combines spatial and temporal information using convolutional neural networks (CNNs) and attention-based long short-term memory (LSTM) networks, and then optimized with k-means clustering to generate a small discrete state space. The temporal lookback window for inputs is adjusted based on the autocorrelation function to ensure that the historical context is meaningful and statistically sound. Explainable AI methods clarify the model's decision-making process, showing the most significant indicators and trends across a wide range of stocks and time horizons. Empirical analyses of data from the U.S. and Indian equity markets indicate that the proposed system outperforms conventional systems in terms of cumulative returns, Sharpe ratios, and other financial performance indicators. The strength of such gains is statistically supported by the Wilcoxon signed-rank test. The resulting framework is therefore a viable prospect of creating interpretable real-time trading agents that can adapt to changing market environments.
